<title>JAPAN: Hewlett-Packard mulls dual samurai bonds - sources.</title>
<headline>Hewlett-Packard mulls dual samurai bonds - sources.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hewlett-Packard Co is considering launching yen/U.S. dollar dual currency samurai bonds in October, underwriting sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>They said the issue volume was expected to be about 30 billion yen, with a duration of about three years.</p>
<p>The coupon would be paid in yen, while redemption would be in U.S. dollars, they said.  </p>
<p>Underwriters said the payment date for the issue was expected to be around October 29.</p>
</text>
